# Keep Docker build context small.
#
# CAUTION: every pattern here removes files from the Docker build context.
# The builder stage compiles the real workspace, so ANY file that a crate
# embeds with `include_str!` / `include_bytes!` MUST NOT be excluded, or
# the build fails with a confusing "No such file or directory" error that
# names a path inside the container rather than the excluded path.
#
# Currently required by the image's dependency closure:
#
#   crates/fabric-frame-transport/src/schema.rs
#     include_str!("../../../docs/spec/wire-protocol-schema.json")
#   crates/fabric-daemon/src/secret_loader/review_response.rs
#     include_str!("../../../../docs/runbooks/workos-infisical-shared.md")
#
# NOTE on Docker's ignore semantics: a pattern like `*.md` matches only
# ROOT-level files; Docker's matcher does not treat `*` as crossing
# directory separators. So `*.md` never removed `docs/**.md` -- the
# runbook was safe for a different reason than it first appeared. The
# explicit `!docs/` exception below documents that intent so a future
# reader does not "simplify" the pattern list and break the build.
target/
.git/
.github/
architecture/
cmd/
deploy/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# Generated documentation output (git-ignored, ~6 MB). Not needed by the
# build and not present in a clean CI checkout.
docs/book/

# Root-level markdown is excluded to keep the context small.
*.md
!README.md

# The daemon embeds docs/runbooks/workos-infisical-shared.md into the
# binary. Keep the whole docs/ tree available to the builder.
!docs/
